# "# " in front of it in a pull request; to switch it off, put the "# " back. Only the owner can merge either
# (this file is a critical path). Netlify's own caching of pages revalidates on every visit, so returning visitors
# see the normal site again as soon as the deploy that switches it off is live. Explained in docs/fallback.md.
# It must stay ABOVE the last line.
#
# /*    /maintenance.html   200!

